        "original_id": "5c07dd2d-0197-5a4f-97f3-9970877a314b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Nordwind\n- People: Pedro del Valle\n- Places: Alsace, Lorraine, northeastern France\n- Topics: World War I, World War II, Banana Wars\n\nFacts:\n- Operation Nordwind was the last major German offensive of World War II on the Western Front.\n- Operation Nordwind began on 31 December 1944 in Alsace and Lorraine in northeastern France, and it ended on 25 January 1945.\n- The Battle of Okinawa lasted 82 days from April 1, 1945, until June 22, 1945.\n- Pedro del Valle served in World War I, in Haiti and Nicaragua during the Banana Wars of the 1920s, and in World War II.\n- Pedro del Valle served at the Battle of Guadalcanal and at the Battle of Okinawa, where he was Commanding General of the 1st Marine Division.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "c9c6190c-c8fa-5f73-8a57-11e66f0df6b5",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Okinawa. Sentence: The 82-day battle lasted from April 1 until June 22, 1945.\nPage: Operation Nordwind. Sentence: Operation North Wind (German: \"Unternehmen Nordwind\" ) was the last major German offensive of World War II on the Western Front.\nPage: Operation Nordwind. Sentence: It began on 31 December 1944 in Alsace and Lorraine in northeastern France, and ended on 25 January.\nPage: Pedro del Valle. Sentence: His military career included service in World War I, Haiti and Nicaragua during the Banana Wars of the 1920s, and in World War II, the Battle of Guadalcanal and Battle of Okinawa (Commanding General of the 1st Marine Division).",
